   "text": {
    "L1": "A double bar graph uses two side-by-side bars for each category.",
    "L2": "The legend tells us which colour belongs to each group.",
    "L3": "Here, cricket has 12 boys and 7 girls, while badminton has 7 boys and 10 girls.",
    "L4": "For badminton and kho-kho, girls total 19 and boys total 12. So, 7 more girls chose them.",
    "L5": "Axis steps must be equal, so equal distances show equal amounts.",
    "L6": "MYTH: Trust a graph without checking its scale. A cut axis can exaggerate a small difference.",
    "L7": "Before believing a graph, read its title, labels, scale and legend, then check the actual numbers.",
    "L8": "Now tap the game that most girls like."
